<title>FRANCE: TF1 head says no TPS changes imminent.</title>
<headline>TF1 head says no TPS changes imminent.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Patrick Le Lay, chairman of broadcaster TF1 and the Televison par Satellite (TPS) digital satellite joint venture, said on Thursday that there where no imminent changes in the TPS share capital.</p>
<p>&quot;The capital of TPS is already very rich, it is not the time to complicate it,&quot; Le Lay told Reuters.</p>
<p>He had earlier told a news conference that he did not exclude that Rupert Murdoch could enter the share capital of TPS, a statement which sent up the TF1 share price by 2.65 percent. The share closed 1.7 percent higher at 537 francs.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
